{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 122, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 4 removed, the skip on edge 3 restores a near-missing input-to-output path, so its gain is much larger (row 16: +73 on C10)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual skip helps cells whose other paths are convolutional, but hurts cells made only of pooling or skips that already lack learnable capacity (rows 13 and 14)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is already none, removing edge 3 leaves the output reachable only through edge 5, so it collapses accuracy (row 38)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is none, removing edge 0 cuts node 2 and node 1 off from the input, so the cell degenerates (rows 19 and 22)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 1 is none, edge 0 is the only feed into nodes 1 and 2, so adding a conv there reconnects the deep part of the cell (rows 90 and 92)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, edge 4 is the only route from the conv stack to the output, so removing it hurts much more (rows 60 and 61)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, edge 1 is node 2's only connection to the input, so removing it disconnects the conv path (row 79)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, removing edge 5 leaves only edge 3 into the output, so the intermediate conv nodes are dropped entirely."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct edge 3, an added conv path from node 1 to the output contributes a larger share of the output signal."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing edge 0 with a skip creates new paths through node 1, whereas replacing an existing conv with a skip removes capacity (row 66 vs rows 64 and 67)."}], "tok": 18005, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_po